1. What this licence covers

"The Software" means the WorkTrust command-line tool in every form in which
Oravtia B.V. distributes it: the "worktrust" package on npm, the "worktrust"
package on PyPI, the scripts served from worktrust.io, the WorkTrust preservation
kit, and the files these install on a computer (including the WorkTrust mod for
Claude Code), together with their documentation. "You" means the person or
organisation that installs or runs the Software.

2. What you may do

Oravtia B.V. grants the licences below free of charge. Each is non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable and revocable, and covers installing and
running the unmodified Software on computers you own or control.

  a. Preserve, for everyone. Anyone, with or without a WorkTrust account, may use
     the Software's "preserve" feature: the local, signed archive of their own AI
     history on their own computer, together with its options (such as --apply,
     --archive, --verify and --summary).

  b. Every other feature, for WorkTrust account holders. A person or organisation
     holding a WorkTrust account may, for as long as they hold it, use every other
     feature the Software ships with the WorkTrust service, including:
       - connecting the computer to their own WorkTrust account ("connect");
       - the counter and the hooks it installs in their AI tools, and the reports
         they send to their own account;
       - importing their own history and data exports to WorkTrust ("history" and
         export import); and
       - anything else in the Software that talks to the WorkTrust service.

  c. Without a WorkTrust account, beyond preserve, you may only install the
     Software and run it to evaluate it.

You may make the copies needed to install and run the Software and a reasonable
number of backup copies. You may read the source code to understand and check
what the Software does on your computer, and you may test it on your own computer
to report a security problem as described in SECURITY.md. Being able to read the
source code gives you no other right.

3. What you may not do

Except as section 2 allows or mandatory law permits, you may not:

  a. copy the Software or any part of it;
  b. modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the Software or any
     part of it;
  c. decompile, disassemble or reverse-engineer the Software;
  d. sublicense, sell, rent, lend, redistribute, publish or otherwise make the
     Software or any part of it available to anyone else;
  e. use the Software, its code or any part of it in another product or service,
     or to build, train or improve a product or service that competes with
     WorkTrust;
  f. remove or change any copyright notice, this licence or any other notice in
     the Software; or
  g. present a modified or rebuilt copy as the Software or as an official
     WorkTrust release.

Nothing in this licence restricts what mandatory law allows a lawful user of a
computer program to do, including the acts permitted by Articles 5 and 6 of
Directive 2009/24/EC as implemented in the Dutch Copyright Act (Auteurswet).

